WEBVTT

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.860
<i>I want to be paired up with
the guy I like for practice!</i>

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.860
<i>I hope my
baby is
born safely</i>

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.860
<i>Please let me stay
happy and healthy</i>

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.480
What?!

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.010
I-I'm sorry! I tripped and...

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.930
Wait...

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.230
Watanabe-san?

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.360
<i>Watanabe Akari and Sakurazaka Shiori...</i>

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.240
<i>I never imagined so many things would 
happen between the two of them and me.</i>

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.620
Oh! Watanabe-san, are you here about 
your partner for the marriage practical?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.780
No, I'm not.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.220
I'm not!

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.640
<b>"Marriage Practical"</b>

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.880
<i>The marriage practical.</i>

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.440
<i>An insane part of our high school's 
curriculum that's about to begin.</i>

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.350
<i>As the name implies, 
male-female pairs are chosen</i>

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.780
<i>to live together as a mock married couple.</i>

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:40.010
<i>Everyone in class is agitated because of it,</i>

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.280
<i>but that's not where my mind is right now.</i>

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.670
Just a little more...

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.670
Just a little more, and 
my bride will be decided!

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.920
Come on, Chloris. Chloris!

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.920
Jiro

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.020
Yes!

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.000
Man, I envy you, Jiro-chan.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.930
Imagine getting excited over a pixel 
art character in this day and age.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.650
You've got it all wrong.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.930
The fact that it's pixel art 
lets the imagination run free.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.260
Just look at <i>RotoSaGa</i>. 
7 is out, and it's got 3D views.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.840
Observe the quality of the newest 
version of Princess Chloris!

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.890
Oh, shut up.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.620
I like the simple innocence 
from back when they did 1.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.340
I guess it does make it 
easier to imagine things...

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.760
But back in 1, you couldn't 
pick the heroine, right?

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.790
Hey.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.960
You're in the way.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.710
Watanabe Akari! She smells so nice.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.190
She really is cute.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.620
How, exactly?

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.080
The way she talks is so unendearing.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.750
She shows so much skin, it's vulgar.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.600
She treats us social outcasts like idiots.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.610
I never, <i>ever</i> want to get 
involved with her type!

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.460
Minami-kun!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.490
I saw you!

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.920
Tenjin Minami, huh?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.120
The newspaper club interviewed 
you in the courtyard, right?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.150
I'm a guy, but even I feel like I'll be 
purified by his sky-high ikemen level!

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.340
Oh, that. Yeah.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.300
It's for the thing they're putting 
you on the cover of, right?

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.020
And he's a good guy on top of that.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.090
Akari keeps saying they must be 
doing a special edition on ikemen.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.970
For us shadow-dwellers, 
he's poison. No, he's absolute evil.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:20.940
Wha?!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:21.970
They wouldn't do that.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.600
B-But Minami-kun, you're really cool, so...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.100
Thanks. It makes me happy to hear that.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.740
She's such an open book.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.570
Talk about a complete 180.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.570
Aw, crap.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.530
Now I've gotta wait to meet my bride.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.530
<b>Jiro</b>

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.400
Jiro-kun.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:46.700
Huh?

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.200
It's finally time for the 
marriage practical, huh?

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.700
Yeah.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.440
I feel sort of nervous.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.050
Is it just me?

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.710
I'm not good with girls, 
so I'm nothing but nerves.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.780
<i>The only girl I can speak with normally</i>

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.720
<i>is my childhood friend and first love.</i>

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.190
<i>They say your first love never comes true,</i>

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.240
<i>but if things can stay like this 
between us forever, that's enough.</i>

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.500
I get shy around strangers, so...

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.730
I hope I'm paired with someone I know well!

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.720
Y-Yeah.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.690
Agency for Cultural Affairs Recommended Demonstration Program 2022

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.690
Marriage Practical Course
Guidance Video

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.690
Now, everyone, pay attention. 
I'm going to begin the explanation.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:26.010
Starting now, you will each live as a pair 
with your partner in the training dorm.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.730
It's furnished and has a kitchen,

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.510
so there's no need to worry 
about day-to-day matters.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:37.330
The sensor installed in the living room will 
continuously monitor your lifestyle and actions.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:37.330
<b>Practical Points</b>

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.840
And here is the most important thing...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.160
As you are all still students, 
your bedrooms are separate.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.430
Fingerprint verification ensures that 
only the room's occupant may enter.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.380
Do not get carried away.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.390
Keep yourselves firmly under control.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.740
<i>What the heck?</i>

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.480
<i>Why even make us do this, then?</i>

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.530
One more thing. 
Regarding the A-rank system...

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.920
<i>There are fifteen guys and 
girls in each of the five classes,</i>

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:09.700
Every month, those ranked in the top 
ten according to their grades...

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.370
<i>meaning there's a 1-in-75 chance 
of being paired with any one person.</i>

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.340
I hope I'm paired with someone I know well!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.180
<i>That's just a fantasy!</i>

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.380
<i>I'm her childhood friend!</i>

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.000
<i>She just finds me easy to talk to 
because she doesn't see me as a guy!</i>

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.580
<i>But if we get paired, then maybe...</i>

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.210
<i>I'll check my luck!</i>

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:28.550
<b>Jiro</b>

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.960
<i>If the hero defeats the boss 
alone with no damage taken,</i>

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.940
<i>he can take the side route to the heroine.</i>

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.680
<i>From there, if you go straight 
through the dungeon...</i>

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.180
<b>Lancia</b>

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.180
<b>Huh?
Do you have a problem with me or something?</b>

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.480
<i>Lancia?!</i>

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.960
<i>No, no.</i>

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.570
<i>This has now purged all my bad luck.</i>

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.940
<i>Only good things can happen now.</i>

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.250
Why is it you?!

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.330
Th-That's kind of what I'd like to ask!

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.080
What?!

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.720
Um, wait just a moment, please.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.880
Let's calm down a bit.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.370
Will you quit talking all formal?
It's creeping me out.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.580
S-Sorry. First, could you let me go?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.570
Now you're <i>too</i> friendly all of a sudden!

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:03.590
You're being unfair.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.540
What a buzzkill. This sucks!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.930
How'd they come up with this pairing, anyway?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.650
It makes no sense at all.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.890
I'm a victim here, too.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.850
What was that?!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.960
It-It's just... It seems like you 
had a preferred partner in mind,

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.240
and I had someone I wanted to be 
paired with, too. That's all I meant.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.240
It's gotta be Sakurazaka-san, right?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.260
<b>BULL'S</b>

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.260
<b>EYE</b>

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.990
You're so easy to read! 
How stupid can you be?

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.280
There's no way she'd ever 
give you the time of day.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.500
<i>I don't want to hear that from you!</i>

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.160
I mean, she's a little plain, but she's cute.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.000
What're you gonna do?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Things might be going really 
well for her right now.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.500
Please, be gentle.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:56.350
M-M-M-Making such wild speculations 
is disrespectful toward her, I feel.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.190
Killjoy.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.520
S-So what if I am?

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.010
Oh, crap!

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.200
If we don't get along, we lose points!

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.750
Then we might get to minus 10,000.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.850
Cut the shit!

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.700
Get along with me!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.410
Right now!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.780
But that attitude! That behavior!

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:18.990
We'll increase our points, get to 
A-rank, and change our pairing!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.130
Ow!

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:23.290
Is that even possible?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.800
Didn't you hear the explanation? 
I can't believe you.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.340
Look at this.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.800
<b>Seishun Academy Third-Years'
Marriage Practical Manual</b>

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:39.480
<b>1-2
At the end of every month, those who score in the top ten (A-rank)
will be granted the right to change pairings among themselves.
In such cases, the consent of everyone involved is required.
2
Regarding Scoring
2-1
 Totals will be reset at the end of the month, and each month will
start at 0 points.</b>

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:36.130
"At the end of every month, 
those who score in the top ten (A-rank)

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.920
will be granted the right to 
change pairings among themselves."

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:39.480
For real?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.440
Minami-kun would never be 
anything less than A-rank.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.350
So let's get that A-rank and switch partners!

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.140
Huh? H-Hey, doesn't that mean...

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.890
No, wait, wait. Hang on just a sec.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:51.780
What?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.410
Reaching A-rank means... you and I...

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.270
Dinner's ready.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.610
Looks delicious.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.750
B-But wouldn't that be kinda dangerous?

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.720
What're you getting all 
embarrassed about, Virgin-kun?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.970
Even if we do things like this...

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.020
everything's totally fine!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.770
<i>H-H-H-H-Her breasts! Breasts! 
What is this soft yet firm warmth?!</i>

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.360
I'll try my very best to be 
the perfect wife for you.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:24.480
I'm counting on you.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.530
W-W-Wait, please! 
You're really o-okay with a guy like me?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.320
Look! It worked!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.860
Let's keep it going!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.640
S-S-Sorry! This is my first 
time doing anything like this.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.120
I'm thirsty. I'm going to 
go buy something to drink.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.360
Then I'll have a strawberry milk.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.170
What?

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.860
We're married! 
You'll buy it for me, won't you?

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.420
Fine.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.030
I just don't want any other 
girl to take Minami-kun away.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.760
I <i>have</i> to try my hardest.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.440
This is my first time doing 
all of this, too, you know...

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.530
Thank you for going along 
with my selfish request.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.700
<i>Seriously?!</i>

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.000
I'm glad I was paired with you, Tenjin-kun.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.080
I'm glad it was you, too, Sakurazaka-san.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.840
So let's use first names, Shiori.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.590
R-Right, Minami-kun.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:37.590
<i>What's with me?</i>

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.600
<i>I thought I didn't care if anything 
happened between me and Sakurazaka!</i>

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.350
Hello! Are you gonna sit here moping forever?

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:54.900
m0 0 l 90 0 l 90 28 l 0 28

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:54.900
<b>Jiro</b>

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:52.160
"I mean, I'm up against 
Tenjin Minami-kun here!"

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.900
"A killjoy virgin like me doesn't 
stand a chance against him!"

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.820
Don't give me a voiceover!

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:59.570
I'm seriously depressed here. 
Please just leave me alone.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:00.740
Well, then...

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.660
Cheer up.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.000
D-D-Don't make fun of people like that!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.530
I'm not making fun of you.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:10.500
Huh?

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:14.340
Come on. Let's actually, 
seriously pretend to be married.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.070
If we reach A-rank, we'll get a happy ending.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:19.760
And it'll be good practice for the 
real thing. What do we have to lose?

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:23.820
The r-real thing? I would never...

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:31.190
Being mopey and indecisive 
won't get you anywhere.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:33.680
Right?

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:40.070
I can't help it. It's not like I've got the 
abundance of experience that you do.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.070
What?!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.410
That's got nothing to do with anything!

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.340
When you do something, 
you've gotta go all-in!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.620
Do you wanna be Virgin-kun forever?

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.170
I'll get it.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.560
Hey.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.620
<i>Jiro-chan, are you free? 
Wanna go to Aniroad?</i>

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.430
Yeah, I'll go! Let's go now!

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.020
That's what's going on, 
so I'll see you later.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.320
Hang on.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:05.930
Huh?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.490
You're leaving when we have negative points?

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:10.500
Well, what am I supposed to do about it?

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.120
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.940
A goodbye kiss.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.810
Do you mean "kisu," the fish 
that tastes good as tempura?

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:18.440
What?!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.500
I'm talking about a goodbye kiss!

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.490
Ki—

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.490
Wha?!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.910
Jiro-chan, are you ready yet?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.160
I guess Virgin-kun wouldn't 
be able to manage it.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.660
Jiro-chan, aren't you ready yet?

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.670
You are just a virgin, after all.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.570
Jiro! Get out here now!

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.960
I guess you'll never have that kind of 
relationship, so you can't help it.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.980
You two virgins should go have fun together.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:41.750
Jiro, did you die?! Or are you dead?!

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.340
Don't get mad at me later, okay?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.000
What took you so long?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.900
If we were at war, I'd be dead already.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:01.850
Sorry.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.400
<i>Crap. I let her rile me up.</i>

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.280
<i>She was treating me like an idiot!</i>

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.670
<i>N-No one said anything about 
it being on the lips...</i>

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:22.380
Jiro-kun. Jiro-kun!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:26.510
Shiori?

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.010
If you don't wake up, I'll give you a kiss!

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:31.000
Then I'm not waking up.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.590
Kiss me.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.290
You really are hopeless. Honestly.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.280
Take that, and that, and that!

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.540
What do you mean, "kiss me"?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.530
Get up and come help me get things ready.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.220
Huh? I-It's morning?

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.410
<i>Crap! I fell asleep here last night?</i>

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:55.380
And don't forget the reason 
we're acting married.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.540
<i>Her lips sure were soft...</i>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.550
<i>No, wait! Shiori's the one I like!</i>

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:02.920
Hey!

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.940
Are you still sitting there?!

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:06.170
I'll knock you into orbit!

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.720
Y-Yes, ma'am! Sorry!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.470
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.470
<i>As all this went on, a week passed.</i>

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.600
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.600
Excuse me.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:22.900
What's this?

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.820
You had class duty today, Yakuin-kun?

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.100
The guy who does asked me to take the 
morning shift because he had stuff to do.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.680
I see. Perfect timing.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:36.320
Come to the faculty office with 
Watanabe-kun after school today.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:37.080
What?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.800
Make sure both husband and wife come.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:40.740
Okay, I will.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:56.690
<i>It must be going well 
between Shiori and Tenjin.</i>

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:58.900
I haven't been there yet.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:01.210
<i>I thought that if I acted like this, she 
might worry about me and say something,</i>

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.180
Really? Then let's go. 
I just know you'll like it.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:01.940
<i>but she hasn't.</i>

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.460
<i>And just thinking that way shows 
how gloomy I am, right?</i>

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:04.970
I'd love to go!

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.950
Okay, it's settled, then!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.960
<i>That back there was probably...</i>

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:08.080
Hey!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.180
What is it, Shiori?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.950
You don't mind, do you? 
We're married, after all!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.810
It's fine with me, but what about him?

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.210
You mean Jiro-kun?

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.540
It's no problem at all! 
He's just an old friend.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.630
You're so cool, and you help me move forward.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.630
<i>My own imaginings are making me cry.</i>

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.090
It's raining? I don't have an umbrella.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:39.220
Don't worry. I have one.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.770
I have to share an umbrella with you?

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.150
No complaining!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.650
Man, today was just another dull day.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.450
I had a good day, though.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.420
My free morning gacha pull got me an 
S-rare card in a school swimsuit costume.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.020
That's thanks to me, right?

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.190
Buy me something.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.410
Can't. I started saving 
up for Marin-chan today.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.360
There it is again. Hashimoto Marin.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.030
Use honorifics for other 
people's girlfriends!

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.170
Marin-san.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:03.460
Very good.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:08.170
In the story for this event, 
Marin-chan makes omelet rice for you,

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.670
and it was so good!

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.930
The taste of it maxed out my love meter!

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.300
"You can't possibly know how 
a JPEG tastes," you say?

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:17.470
Fool! A JPEG is meant to be 
savored with the occipital lobe!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:18.430
Stop for a sec.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.310
<b>Occipital Lobe</b>

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.310
Parietal Lobe

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.310
Frontal Lobe

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.310
Temporal Lobe

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.760
By the way, this is the part I mean.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.430
Move!

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.020
Move! You're in the way!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.430
I might be late today.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:28.040
Okay... Why?

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.480
I'm going to karaoke, 
and Minami-kun is coming!

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.340
Oh, is that so?

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:33.450
Later!

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:37.870
Wait! Wait, Watanabe.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:38.920
What is it?

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:42.160
I just remembered. The teacher said 
we need to go to the faculty office.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.460
It's about the practical.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.300
Oh... I guess we have no choice, then.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.750
Take care of it solo, 'kay?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.260
Hey!

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.530
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.640
This really was the worst day ever.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.450
To hell with that!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.100
Your childhood friend is 
the pure, sweet type,

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.470
and your mock wife is a hot gyaru?!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.140
You've got a flower in each hand!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.960
Are you the hero of a 
harem anime or something?!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.770
Oh, shut up.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:07.740
I could live on the carbon dioxide 
Akari-chan exhales, personally.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.880
If anything, I am carbon dioxide itself.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:11.650
Huh?

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.910
Meaning no one needs me.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.160
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.160
No, it's absolutely necessary.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.320
The marriage practical isn't playing 
at being friends. It's coursework.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.160
It's necessary for graduation.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
<b>71st</b>

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Kasugahara Kyo

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Sangamori Hatsune

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
<b>72nd</b>

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Yakuin Jiro

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Watanabe Akari

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Kaizuka Yoshitake

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:28.670
Nakahara Miyako

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:26.080
Your score hasn't gone up or down 
for a week. It's stayed at zero.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.670
At this rate, you really 
won't be able to graduate.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:32.920
Talk things over with Watanabe-san so that 
you can strive to be a happily married couple.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.180
Unlimited Time

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.180
Karaoke
 30 minutes
 100 yen
 Unlimited Time
 1000 yen

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.430
Minami-kun, you're super good at this!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:39.750
And your English is so good! I was surprised!

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.900
Thanks. But there aren't 
many songs I can sing.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.840
My voice is all hoarse already.

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:43.900
Wanna sing together?

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.190
Of course you can!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.190
What did you pick, Watanabe?

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:46.670
Go, Akari!

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:48.010
Oh, this is it! Higashino Kana-chan!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:48.830
Here.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.690
Huh? I don't know if I can keep singing.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.690
I've heard you sing before. You're good.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:52.830
Really?

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.900
Then maybe I'll give it my best this time.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.200
This rain just isn't stopping.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.220
It's easy to say to try to be 
a happily married couple,

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:07.210
but she's probably off having 
fun with her real love interest.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.060
Hey, Akari is tired from singing.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.970
Why don't we go take a little 
breather in the next room?

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.180
<i>What am I thinking?!</i>

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.500
<i>There's no helping it.</i>

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.940
<i>I'll just deal with getting wet,</i>

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.200
<i>buy dinner from a convenience 
store, and head home.</i>

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.690
Oh? You're still here at school?

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:31.130
Shio— Sakurazaka?! 
What are you doing here so late?

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.190
We had a committee meeting today.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.440
May I sit next to you?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.110
S-Sure.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.590
This rain isn't letting up, huh?

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:42.700
Do you have an umbrella?

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.460
I forgot it!

